[center][size=6][b][color=#d29cff]T4RG3T5[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][i][color=#b44cff]Lock on. Stay on. Dark Souls 1-inspired targeting for the modern outlander.[/color][/i][/size]

T4rg3t5 is a full lock-on targeting system for OpenMW, built around fast target acquisition, readable combat feedback, and a completely rebuilt third-person combat camera.

Lock onto an eligible combat target and T4rg3t5 handles facing, directional target switching, visibility, range, camera composition, and target feedback. The camera is collision-aware, shoulder-switching, independently smoothed, and extensively configurable.

[color=#8f3fc7][b]Target acquisition listens to OpenMW's combat-target updates instead of scanning every actor in the world. The hot path came through the barbershop for a fade.[/b][/color]

[url=https://youtu.be/OwHE_Or-Ps0][b][color=#d29cff]Watch the 1.0 combat demo[/color][/b][/url]

[b][color=#d29cff]Assign a keybinding under Settings → T4rg3t5 → Target Lock Core, or the mod will be (mostly) useless.[/color][/b]
[/center]

[size=5][b][color=#8f3fc7]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#b44cff]Souls-style Lock Camera[/color][/b] — Collision-aware orbiting, automatic shoulder switching, configurable framing, FOV, smoothing, and lock-loss behavior.[/*]
[*][b][color=#b44cff]Smart Targeting[/color][/b] — Visibility-aware acquisition, directional flick switching, combat auto-lock, dead-target switching, and range validation.[/*]
[*][b][color=#b44cff]Combat Tracking[/color][/b] — Automatic facing, first- and third-person support, and weapon/sheathing awareness.[/*]
[*][b][color=#b44cff]Target Feedback[/color][/b] — 31 included markers, distance scaling, hit bounce, and continuous health coloring across six configurable colors.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#8f3fc7]For Mod Authors[/color][/b][/size]

T4rg3t5 1.0 exposes a documented player interface, live settings, target-change events, trigger support, and integration examples.

